  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "Find $AB,$ if $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |  |",
  "worked_solution": "Here, $A$ is $3\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix.  \n\nThere is $1$ column in matrix $A$ and $1$ row in matrix $B$, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{\u2713}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{3\\times 2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1\\cdot 1 & 1\\cdot (-2) \\\\ 2\\cdot 1 & 2\\cdot (-2) \\\\ (-2)\\cdot 1 & (-2)\\cdot (-2)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
